      "body": {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Nitrogen belongs to group 15 of the periodic table. In industrial processes, nitrogen is typically obtained by cooling air until it becomes a liquid. Liquid nitrogen is commonly used for rapid cooling purposes. In laboratory settings, nitrogen can be generated by slowly heating a solution of ammonium nitrite."
          },
          {
            "type": "equation",
            "latex": "\\ce{NH4NO2_{(aq)} ->[\\Delta] N2_{(g)} + H2O_{(l)}}",
            "text_alt": "NH₄NO₂(aq) →(Δ) N₂(g) + H₂O(l)",
            "book_errors": [
              "H₂O(l)",
              "H2O_{(l)}"
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "callout",
            "tone": "correction",
            "title": "Book correction",
            "text": "This equation is not balanced: the left side has 4 H and 2 O atoms, the right side only 2 H and 1 O. The balanced equation is NH₄NO₂(aq) → N₂(g) + 2H₂O(l)."
